Jeff DeMaagd wrote:
> 
> 
> I have a stock installation of Red Hat 5.1 from my official CD.  So
> far, the three times I've reconfigured and recompiled my kernel, the
> new kernel boots just fine, but the console won't accept keyboard input
> in any case.

Most likely you forgot to configure CONFIG_VT_CONSOLE while you are
not running an embedded system with a remote, or none, access.
The other candidate will be forgotten CONFIG_UNIX98_PTYS.

Besides 2.2 kernels have some requirements on a user space.  Minima
are listed in Documentation/Changes file in kernel sources.  No, you
do not have to run 6.0 to satisfy these requirements.

  Michal


