On Mon, 6 Sep 1999, Imran Siddiq wrote:

> > Has anyone seen a problem where Gnome locks up your system?

It's probably not Gnome itself. It's probably the X server. If you have
another machine networked to your Alpha, try logging in from the other
machine with telnet. 

It'd be useful to know if Linux is crashing completely, or if X is getting
killed and just trashing the console. If you can log in from the network
(or a serial terminal) then you can use the reboot command as root to
take the system down correctly to avoid abrupt power downs. 

If the whole machine is locking, then I'd say that your problem has much
less to do with Gnome, and more to do with a bad kernel configuration, or
maybe memory troubles, or something. 

