For those that are interested here are some results which
i got from my first use of the Compaq c compiler (ccc)
on my XL300 (A 300Mhz 21164 with 2Mb level three cache).

The program is a model of unsaturated soil water flow, it
uses pow and sqrt a lot (80 % of the CPU time) in method 0.
With method 1 pre-gererated look-up tables (300 rows deep) are
used in stead.

Method  time [sec]      Description
1,      17.024368,      egcs + cpml + lookup-tables
0,      29.208752,      egcs + cpml
1,      13.000560,      ccc  + cpml + lookup tables
0,      19.815728,      ccc  + cpml


As you can see the speed-ups are between 30 and 50%. I have
not been able to use the -ifo option (part of the -fast option)
so that should give some extra speedup (i have to rearrange the code for
that). Without cpml (or ffm) run times for method 0 go
up to 90 seconds.
                                     
