Christian Iseli wrote:
> 
> Hi folks,
> 
> Here is a (maybe stupid) question that's been bugging me for a while: whenever
> I upgrade my C library (rpm -U glibc*2.1.2preX*), the next time I reboot, the /
> (root directory) cannot be properly unmounted, which leads to a rather lengthy
> (though harmless) fsck upon reboot.
> 
> What is causing it, and can it be avoided ?
>

I believe the fsck is caused by a lingering reference count to the old
shared libc from running daemons. It conceivably could be avoided by
killing/restarting all processes except init but that's hardly worth the
trouble.

