The only Symbios chip based boards (875 and later) that will work in Digital
UNIX are ones sold by Compaq or IntraServer (since we wrote the driver).
The message "using unsupported 875 chip" indicates that our driver did not
recognize the 875 board as one licensed from IntraServer and therefore the
PSIOP driver (the one designed for the 810 chip) picked up the board and is
running it as if it is an 810 (i.e. it is not running Ultra SCSI, it's
running the board in SCSI-2 mode).  If it had been an 895 or 896 based
board, it would not have run at all if it wasn't licensed....

ok, lets head back to *Linux* now....

cheers,
