> I was reading an old Unix book and it
> mentioned the stty command but the linux man file talks about printing???

You mean this:

          stty - change and print terminal line setting

This "print" means "print on your stdout" (which is usually somehow 
connected to your display - but not always).

> Also someone mentioned you could configure your kernel to run 386
> binaries???

Probably it is already configured.  Try to run this netscape.
If failed check complaints in /var/log/messages.  You need the following
packages installed:

em86
em86-x86
em86-baselibs
em86-X11libs

Otherwise you need EM86 support (a module is fine) in your kernel
and www.alphalinux.org likely has some writeups on the topic.

  Michal


