Hello all,
	I have kept my AlphaPC 164LX running RH4.2 up to now.
Over this long weekends, I downloaded the RH6.0 from sunsite.unc.edu
and tried to install it on my Alpha. Finally I could get it running but
with problems. Here are the followings:

	Basic info:
		AlphaPC 164LX
		RAM 128 MB
		hard disk partitions:
				/dev/sda1	msdos
				/dev/sda2	Linux Native
				/dev/sda3	Linux swap
				/dev/sda4	winnt
				
				/dev/sdb1	Linux Native
				/dev/sdc1	Linux Native
				
	RH4.2 was originally installed on /dev/sda2. What I did for RH6.0
was to upload the RH6.0 to /dev/sdc1 and tried to install it on /dev/sdb1
( mount point / (root) for RH60), while keeping RH4.2 on /dev/sda2 for now.
After making the three diskettes, MILO (linload.exe), Boot, and Ramdisk,
I went to the AlphaBios setup and added on OS as LinuxFloppy. So I have
three OSs after the AlphaBios initialization:
	Linux/RH4.2
	Window NT
	LinuxFloppy
	
Selecting LinuxFloppy and following the installation instructions,
I couldn't upgrate the RH4.2 to RH6.0. Instead, I tried to install RH6.0.

Installation was finally "successful" by getting " Congratulations. The
installation is complete". However, I could not boot from /dev/sdb1 by 
using (at the MILO> prompt)
	boot sdb1:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sdb1
After rebooting using Linux/RH4.2, I found that there is no
vmlinux.gz under root / on /dev/sdb1. Instead, I found vmlinuz under /boot. 
So I used 
	boot sdb1:boot/vmlinuz root=/dev/sdb1
on the second time to reboot RH6.0 and then it was ok. And then
I copied the MILO (linload.exe) to /dev/sda1 using 
dd if=/dev/fd0 of=/dev/sda1 bs=1440k
		
	The question is why there is no vmlinux.gz under root as usually it does
even for "successful and complete installtion"?


	The second problem is that I have to type the boot command at the MILO 
prompt for each reboot. I tried to edit the LinuxFloppy setup as follows,

	Boot Name:	Linux/RH6.0
	OS ?	:	disk0, partition 1	linload.exe
	OS Path	:	CD			milo
	OS options: boot sdb1:boot/vmlinuz root=/dev/sdb1
				
but it did work and I always get the MILO prompt.

Does anyone have experience with these two problems? Or can anyone help me on 
these?


Thanks,

Sun


