There has been support in the SRM code pool for the 53c896 for around 8-12
months now...what problem are you having?  Since it's just running async at
the SRM, my understanding is that the code to make the 896 run was pretty
much "if deviceid=896, pretend it's a 53c810".  Also at the SRM there are no
checks relating to who's the manufacturer of the board (i.e. at the SRM any
manufacturer's 896 based adapter aught to run).

Some of the various hardware groups do maintain their own SRM code and
snapshot the main pool periodically, but given how long the 896 support has
been in, I'd be surprised if any current platform didn't have it (something
that is EOL like multia may be a different story).

cheers,
Kevin

