hmmm, what version of the SRM firmware are you running?  It looks like V5.5
is the latest (http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/).  We don't
have an XP1000 here, so I can't check for you, but if you are running V5.5
and don't see the drives, you can do some debugging.  Start by doing a "show
pk*" from the >>> prompt.  This should list all Symbios based adapters (and
a few others if they are in the system).  If you do not see a PK assignment
for your 896, try a "show config|more" from the >>> prompt.  Then look for
an unlabelled device, which rather than a descriptive name like Symbios 875,
just lists the PCI vendor and device ID's.  The Symbios Vendor ID is 0x1000
and the 896's device ID is 0xb, so I think it's listed as either 1000000B or
000B1000.  If it is showing up as a vendorID deviceID pair, then SRM is not
executing code for that device (i.e. the device is not supported).

Only Tru64 and OpenVMS do the checks for the boards...there are no checks in
either SRM or AlphaBIOS.

cheers,
Kevin

