Hello!

> I have a AXP pci-33MB (one of the ones with the old 166 chip)
> The serial ports are not standard, so I'm not able to connect a modem to
> this thing, since I don't have the manual I'm at a loss.
The manual is not so informative anyway :(

> Does anyone have the correct pinouts so that I can connect a modem to this
> guy??  i.e. pin1 on MB goes to pinx on a normal serial port :)
OK. The cable you need is a 9 pin flat ribbon cable. The you need a plug for
the motherboard and a SUB-D connector. Both should be the form so that the
cable can be "squeezed" onto them (I don't know the correct english
expression for this, sorry).
The pin assignment is then (motherboard to 9-pin numbers)
 1-1 2-6 3-2 4-7 5-3 6-8 7-4 8-9 9-5

Older PC-ATs used to have those, newer PCs use the "straight" wiring, i.e.
1-1 2-2 3-3 4-4...

> TIA
CU
