It's a multia, sometimes referred to as a UDB (universal desktop box).  It
was designed primarily for NT and Linux.

You'll find references to it in the howto's/faq's.

#The sucker seems to run pretty darned hot.

Before reading the "Multia" bootup screen, this comment gave it away... :)

#to hang? I presume that it's due to the battery being dead? This 
#machine's been sitting on the shelf for a couple of years.

It's a common problem and could be the case.

#It has no hard drive and does not appear to have room inside for one. I
#presume that this machine was designed to be a diskless client? I
#presume I can set this machine up to boot diskless? 

no, it uses notebook sized hard-drives.  There is actually a bracket that
you can use to install a small drive into it.  Of course, with the heat it
already has, as well as the tight space, you might be better off going
with some external drive source :)

Thats about all I can answer, I just now got mine and plan on attemting
some diskless configuration.  But I have yet to do so because I need to
buy some stinking Parity Ram.  If anyone has any they'd part with cheaply
on this list, let me know :)

