here's a question for ya:

ripping CD's to WAV files using CDParanoia I am always getting SCSI
timeouts. it will hang the entire SCSI bus and just sit there and reset till
the cows come home.
I tried this on a newly formatted drive and it seems better, except I still
get them from time to time, esp when I load the drive down with more than
just that one process....

even when I am encoding the WAV files to mp3 I get the same type of errors
on the newly formatted drive.

System description:

Alpha 164SX 533mHz w/ 384mb ram
1 Adaptec 2940W controller (handles the CDReader and CDWriter)
1 Adaptec 2940UW controller (handles the hard drives)
drives:
2x 9.1GB IBM Ultra2's (one of these is the root for linux and keeps
messing up)
2x 18.2GB Compaq 10k rpm's SCSI-3
1x 4.3GB Compaq 10k rpm (this is the drive that works for the most part)
1x 540mb seagate (for swap)
-The drives are in an external case w/ a SCSI-3 cable that runs to the
Adaptec 2940UW controller

-also added about 4 more fans than stock to the ATX case
-and added 5 more fans to the external SCSI case
  both ran too hot without them

running RH Linux 6.0
I upgraded the kernel from the stock 2.2.5-16 to 2.2.5-22 this morning
the system's been running (with the reboots from the SCSI timeouts) for
about 2 weeks now. typically it sits up 24/7
-gotta love free electricity in dorm rooms =)

any ideas of what to do?
thanks
Kurt Ludwig


