First of all, make sure you have the XFree 3.3.5 packages from the errata
installed.  This seems to fix the random xfs crashes on some machines.
Otherwise, you can install all but the TTF fonts directly into the
XF86Config, and use xfstt (from contrib.net) for TTF fonts.  This works on
the PWS 600au I have on my desk.  We're working to get the xfs bugs worked
out.

