I had RH5.2 NFS working fine too, but only on 21164 based
systems so even though you're on a DS10(21264), if you use
a recent kernel, it should be OK. I moved to RH6.0 within
a month of it's release to allow easy upgrade to newer kernels.
It does have it's own set of problems but they don't cause
me any real trouble. I run mostly my own codes so I don't
see many of the problems others report with RH6.0.

> May I ask what is ncr53c8xxx and the Becker's site? tulip is the driver
> for the adapter?
> 
> Carlos


The ncr53c8xx driver is for NCR/Symbios SCSI adapters. There
is a bug in recent kernels that makes the udelay() macro behave
erratically so that sometimes the delay is off by a factor of
two. The ncr53c8xx driver uses this macro to determine the clock
frequency of the card and gets bad clock rates for these cards,
but only sometimes...

Donald Becker maintains the tulip driver. I found that using the
driver that come with the standard Linux kernel does not support
the 21143 in the DS10 properly. By that, I mean it will hang under
heavy load. See: http://cesdis1.gsfc.nasa.gov/linux/ and follow
links to latest code. I've moved GigaBytes with the current driver
without trouble.


Wes


