Did this to my SX before...
you need to get an older version of SRM to do this...
the problem with the newer versions of SRM is that it doesn't fit all on one
disk.
you need to get an older version of them and downgrade to that.
boot up in failsafe mode with the older version SRM disk and install it that
way
that was the big stumbling block for me when I upgraded (downgraded) to it.
Once you actually have the SRM.ROM loaded in, you can then upgrade the rest
of
the SRM files to the latest version.
Kurt
-been there done that
oh! also the options for the other loaders don't really do anything in
AlphaBIOS on
the SX series....


