Once the machine is up and running Linux type this (as root):

swriteboot /dev/sda /boot/bootlx -f3

the /dev/sda assumes you're doing this on a SCSI disk so please substitute
the correct device. the -f3 is only needed if you made partition 3 the
entire disk.

Oh, you disk partition the disk with BSD disklabels right?

--rdp

