> haven't gotten around to installing Linux on my SX yet, though.  So it's not
> a problem with the chip not being "Alpha friendly".

The Soundblaster PCI64/128 ES137x based cards don't work in all Alphas.
That is why I claim they are not Alpha friendly. As I said before, it
works on some motherboards/pci configurations but not others. I wouldn't
call this reliable enough to recommend it to anyone.

You might want to ask Thomas Sailer (the guy who wrote the Linux driver)
about them, he is aware of the problems.

Anyway, I'm going to try the hoontech.com cards. They have excellent
sound-to-noise ratios and look pretty cool. Work well under Linux/Intel..

Daniel


