Rafael Noas wrote:

> Hi all,
>
> Can any1 help me with the installation of the aboot on the hdd on a
> alphaserver 1200?
> I created the two floppies from generic.img and ramdisk.img and
> "succesfully" install redhat linux 6.0 on the box but I don't know how to
> install the aboot on the hdd.
>
> Any1?
>
> Thanks in advance
>
> Rafael Noas

Start Linux using the boot floppy:
(X=the number of the root partition)

>>> boot dva0 -file vmlinux.gz -flags root=/dev/sdX

Login as root, and type:
(again, X= the root partition)

# /sbin/swriteboot /dev/sdX /boot/bootlx

After all this, you should be able to edit your SRM variables:
(replace dka0 with your first boot drive, X still equals the root partition
number)

set bootdef_dev dka0
set boot_file X/boot/vmlinux-2.2.5-16
set boot_osflags root=/dev/sdX

And if all goes well, you can then boot the machine by typing:

>>> b <enter> (or >>>boot <enter>)

Hope this helps!

Chris Kloiber



