Mark Henry wrote:

> Hi,
>
> Wondering if anyone can tell me how to format the small fat partition -
> intended to hold MILO - as fat?  I can't boot to a dos disk - obviously -
> wrong platform - and I can't see the partition in the boot selector menu and
> so assumed it wasn't formatted properly.
>
> In fdisk I have specified the fs type as fat <32M (#4) but just don't know
> how to format it!
>
> Thanks!
>
> Mark

No need to format it. Put the Milo disk in the floppy drive and type:

# cat /dev/fd0 > /dev/sda1

(or hda1 if it's an IDE drive)
It's ugly, but it works.

If you really want to format it the right way, try:

# mkdosfs /dev/sda1

Chris Kloiber



