I can recommend the book. Note that it is not targeted at any one operating
system. Most of the examples are written for both VMS and Tru64, but the
focus is on the generic instruction set. There is not much information on
how to interface your code to the operating system (like I/O), but if you
want to write some specialized subroutines, this book will take you almost
all the way.

I say almost, because the calling conventions on alpha are quite complex,
and really not meant to be implemented "by hand". The book recommends to
make a stub in C or Fortran with all parameters you want, compile it, and
use the assembly listing as a starting point.

/Lennart

