Huch, no I can't but I had it running on UX, too.
It was ~2.2.3. Maybe you can try a different PCI slot
(could it be a PCI-PCI bridge problem ?).

I've never programmed PCI but I as far as I know I see no reason
why the card has to know it's own IRQ at all. The only thing that's
interesting for the card is which of the four IRQ-Lines on the
PCI-bus it should use (INT A - INT D).
The PCI-BIOS assigns the IRQ's to the IRQ lines, so the card uses
normally the INT A-line all the time and has nothing to know about
the IRQ-Mapping.

[Maybe this is totally wrong, I hope that somebody will correct me in
this case, it seems consistend.]


