Powerstorm is a marketing term.

It covers a bunch of disparate hardware, including Permedia, TGA, TGA-2,
Integraph and E&S hardware.

Permedia bits are already available.

TGA support is available (though not optimal), that runs on
some of the TGA hardware.

I recently packaged all the device dependent X code Digital developed 
for the SFB/TGA/TGA2 and provided it to the XFree86 organization. For 
various legal reasons, it is unlikely we can ever do likewise for the 
Integraph or E&S hardware.  Please don't ask me: I've already looked into 
it as much as I can.

People are encouraged to help XFree86 integrate this code into their
release.
				- Jim Gettys


