On Fri, 24 Sep 1999, Kirk R. Erichsen wrote:

  Paul,
  
  The latest AlphaBIOS includes support for the whole family of DAC960
  DAC1164 RAID controllers IN firmware (drivers are embedded).  The config
  tool is of cource console based (ARC console app) and can be found on the
  Compaq/DEC FTP site.

Would that count for AlphaBIOS on non-DEC designed boards aswell? Eg,
Samsung UX? (worst comes to the worst i can always boot from floppy)
  
  SISL (Interrupt redirection) is not supported by the AlphaBIOS nor by the
  SRM.  The functionality is only implemented (thus far) on PC hardware and
  none of the RISC systems employ it (probably because of the scale RISC
  systems usually use "real" host based RAID controllers with their own I/O
  connectors). 
  
damm... i was hoping it would be supported in some way, as i have a
mix of lvd and uw drives. ah well.

  Good luck,
  
  --Kirk  

thanks for the info kirk.

regards,
