I'm @ UMass Lowell for school right now (by the obvious email address)
running the pump client. Works fine here on this network, although I am not
sure what type of server they are using to run the DHCP (for all I know,
they're using the router to do it). but here, anyways, pump works just fine.
Anyone that is subscribed to any other more general redhat lists should post
that on those lists as a general test if it hasn't been mentioned before. I
haven't tried it on any other archetecture revision of RH6.0 yet...

I came up with the solution figuring that DHCPCD was a more generic client
