Maurice,

Could you elaborate on the sorts of issues you've seen?
It would be helpful to compile a list of problems that
people have encountered so that one can see on a single
list, the sorts of problems that exist.

What I've seen:

1. Gnome is broken.
2. ping/traceroute were broken but are supposed to be fixed now.
3. The lp package is broken. Haven't looked for a fix.
4. Others have had trouble with xfs but it works for me.(YMMV)
5. Others have mentioned missing/broken text consoles,
   rxvt I think. I live with KDE's term.
6. I've run into some bugs in egcs-1.1.2 and have
   switched to gcc-2.95.1.
7. I run newer kernels than are supplied by RH6.0
   to pick up some kernel fixes I need.

I've built my SW on RH6.0 and have no trouble running
quite large problems on my DS10's or XP1000. I also
use my PC164LX as an I/O node to feed data to all my
systems (Alpha, Intel, RS/6000) without trouble. I've
moved TB's of data. I also burn CD-R's and CD-RW's, 
and have quite large amounts of disk attached.

Maybe I've been lucky or just don't use alot of the
various packages but overall I've been satisfied with
RH6.0.

Oh, one other thing, I don't bother with sound so that
may be one reason I've done OK.

I also tend to use accessories/adapters that are known 
to work.


Wes


