As others are already commenting explicitly on the specific issues, I will 
instead respond in a "customer satisfaction" point of view.
We have sold a lot of Alphas to a lot of different people, so they can run 
Linux on them.
Almost universally their experience with Red Hat 6.0 has been a negative one.
  I quote one of our customers, who is a software developer (database 
tools) who wrote me just the other day:
"I just upgraded one of my machines to RedHat 6.0 and the system has 
crashed daily ever since.  I suspect RedHat is being driven by the 99% of 
their customers who use x86, and their alpha configurations do not get 
tested.  Outside of RedHat, is the alpha version of Linux getting adequate 
development attention?"

I would say this is a typical "Out of box experience" with 6.0


