My threshold for acceptance has more to do with how I use
the systems. I don't expect Alphas to be my main system, only
compute nodes for running my own parallel applications. That
means the base system has to behave and the compilers have
to work. If RH are able to build their distribution on
it, that's about equivalent to what I expect from it. In 
other words, I use Alphas for what they're good at, FP
computation, not for documents, web access, etc. 

I use an Intel RH6.0 for my main system because they work
better at those other things and since most of the SW is
still developed on 32 bit systems, 64 bit systems will
be continually "bitten" by that development path, always
a release behind to fix the bugs that keep creeping back
into the code due to programmers not understanding the
64 bit issues because they don't use 64 bit systems.

A side note:

I finally got my hands on a 500mhz Athlon. It is the fastest
x86 box I've used. Running RH6.0 on it now.


Wes


